# Hyperbolic Arakelov Theory of `Spec ℤ`

Umbrella for the Arakelov geometry of the surface of `Spec ℤ` whose archimedean fibre is `ℍ³` with
the degree geodesic: image distances in Arakelov coordinates; the carriers of B118′ — dilation limits
of twisted carriers, carriers of bounded geometry, along a loxodromic axis and along an end of bounded
self-energy (conical ends included), the boundary of a group convergent at `½` (no parabolic elements,
points of discontinuity), and embeddings into compact and finite-volume quotients; the spherical
structure of the archimedean compensation and the plastic crossing; the discriminant diagonal of
locked dampings; the mass obstruction to scalar locking and ordered Gram coupling on smooth packets;
the finite places as Bruhat–Tits trees with the adelic Green formula; the arithmetic-unit obstruction
to descending a degree ladder and its reconstruction from positive twisted tree fibres; a discrete
adelic arithmetic group whose finite Weyl conjugate retains every original degree in the projective
vertex carrier, with commuting prime Hecke operators retaining neighbour multiplicities; the full
minimal branch of the actual finite-place walk Green kernels; the least nonnegative single-point
Green kernel for sums of adjacency operators on finite products, with uniform collapse under
unweighted exhaustion of the primes; a nonzero least Green kernel on the full finite adelic
product for `p⁻²`-weighted adjacency, with a proved convergence domain and divergent constant rows;
an exact ground-state energy decomposition and intrinsic coercivity on every finite configuration;
Dirichlet inverse exhaustion proving symmetry and strict covariance positivity of the global kernel;
their prime-fibre sum recovering
arithmetic contact, and a marked potential for the torsion different; translation-averaged prime
Green channels with one arithmetic mass clock recovering Weil's form on all real compact smooth
packets, monotonically from below with a uniform Sobolev error, a sharp square-root prime-capacity
threshold, uniform recovery on growing support windows, and a strictly positive first variation
giving the exact damping-error scale on every nonzero packet; the full Weil functional
as a scalar-renormalized tower of primitive-pair Poincare diagonals; the foliation
classifications, local critical Green product, archimedean digamma–Robin–orbit bridge, and
obstruction theorem proving that Weil's diagonal is not the finite part of one torus-invariant
glued object on the adelic carrier; and the
weight of the orientation cover over ℤ. See `HyperbolicArakelovTheory/README.md`.
-/
